{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/104617-why-not-use-the-fomori-mockeries-in-all-the-gamelines","id":104617,"title":"Why not use the Fomori (Mockeries) in all the Gamelines?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-02T22:48:54-07:00","id":104617,"title":"Why not use the Fomori (Mockeries) in all the Gamelines?","content":"Just curious but it seems to me that Fomori (for the sake of the thread I will call them Mockeries because it is a term not seated in a specific culture) would fit with most of the other gamelines as good general Antagonists. You don't even really have to worry about contaminating your game with crossover stuff. Vampires already acknowledges evil spirits exist. Sorcerers interact with them and the Baali, Setites, and Tzimisce have a long history with interacting with wicked spirits. So you don't really loose or dilute anything in a vampire game by having Mockeries.<br /> <br /> Mages ties deeply with the Umbra and evil spirits. They also handle misc supernatural situations and could even include their own setting spins on them with various taints/flaws as signs of Paradox. Nephandi and Umbral Dark Lords would definitely have Mockeries as part of their repertoire.<br /> <br /> Wraith I think would benefit from the mystery added by inhuman spirits, and I'm quite interested in mentioning the souls of those possessed by evil spirits after they die. I would imagine some would have the evil spirit usurp/merge with their Shadow.<br /> <br /> Mummy already has a form of Mockery called a 4 Jar, from cultists bound to evil spirits with a lesser form of immortality.<br /> <br /> Changeling seems the like the gameline that most wants to separate from the rest of the CWOD. But still Demon possessed mortals are always a good prodigal to throw in, and they would have as much to do with the game as mortal ghosts. They also have a tie in with the Fomorians, as it was implied that the Fomorian invasion had Mockeries and Fomorian fae among their Horde.<br /> <br /> For Hunter Mockeries seems like they would be a major simple foe for the Imbued, they rank up there with Zombies and Draculers. In fact I think they are more fitting as foes then Werewolves and Mages.<br /> <br /> The Middle Kingdom Setting already has them as the General Antagonists for everyone as the Yama Kings are everyone's foes and they employ them. So the Wan Kuei, Hengeyokai, Hsien, Mages, and Demon Hunters already all include the local Mockeries (Bakemono) as their General Antagonists.<br /> <br /> Demon has an interesting fit since its the only gameline that says only the Underworld Exists rather thenother Spirit Worlds, which is ironic and terrible planning in my opinion since their background story is the most accommodating to other realms of existence. But Demons already use lesser spirits like making Elementals with Rituals, and Earthbound would fit perfectly with using Mockeries as minions.<br /> <br /> To me it just fits the CWOD in General. You don't need to know Cosmology beyond evil spirits exist and they sometimes possess people.<br /> <br /> In my opinion this makes things like the new Book of the Wyrm that is coming out a good resource for all gamelines. Even when I was just getting started in the CWOD one of the major draws to getting the other gamelines was mining them for NPCs. The Cyborgs and Revenants in the Werewolf Revised Core was an excellent example of including supernaturals without needing to mess with crossover cosmologies. And in my opinion Draculers fit as antagonists in other gamelines because they are mostly athiest blood sucking corpses, they don't really contradict anyones cosmology.<br /> <br /> Damn I had to retype this from a pic on my phone because my computer froze... :P oiyeee!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T22:52:49-07:00","id":104620,"title":"","content":"I do in fact use Fomori in all spheres. I just ran a rather successful story arc involving fomori in my Sabbat LARP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T23:55:55-07:00","id":104661,"title":"","content":"Well, you can, but canon-wise<br /> <br /> Fomori have very little reason to deal with vampires, pretty much ever. Vampires are doing a pretty good job shitting up their own souls and making the world terrible. Plus, Banes get fucked if they try to possess vampires.<br /> <br /> Wraiths have enough nastiness to deal with, and Banes can't enter the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Fomori are originally intended as cannon fodder for werewolves (one of the most powerful character types), and thus might be too strong for changelings (one of the weakest character types). However they do have ties to House Balor so there are perfectly good reasons to use them.<br /> <br /> Hunters? Sure. <br /> <br /> Mages? They work great as Nephandic underlings.<br /> <br /> Kuei-Jin? Well, since KoE are basically Vampire-Wraith-Werewolves, sure, why not. <br /> <br /> Demons are tricky. There isn't really a reason you couldn't...but it doesn't really jive with Demon. Fighting gross monsters just isn't what Demon is really about. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T00:23:26-07:00","id":104673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/104617-why-not-use-the-fomori-mockeries-in-all-the-gamelines?p=104661#post104661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you can, but canon-wise<br /> <br /> Fomori have very little reason to deal with vampires, pretty much ever. Vampires are doing a pretty good job shitting up their own souls and making the world terrible. Plus, Banes get fucked if they try to possess vampires.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Fomori are created from all walks of life, you can be just exposed to tainted products which makes you vulnerable to bane possession, or just get possessed because your life is close to the trauma/pollution/emotion the bane feeds off of. Most Fomori aren't aware at all of the spirit world of the supernatural, they are usually just know they have become a monster. Vampires are regularly tied to all the basic human sins and misery. So they could easily encounter fomori at night clubs, among addicts, or just about anywhere on any level of the Underworld. Ferectoi, those born as Fomori, basically are often born into influential families and become things like business men politicians and mobsters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wraiths have enough nastiness to deal with, and Banes can't enter the Underworld. </div> </div> </div>Not true. Banes usually just don't go into the Underworld, but many Umbral spirits travel in the Underworld, For example Cat and Owl spirits have been known to go to the Dark Umbra, and in the Middle Kingdom Banes live in the Hellish Yin Realms. Apophis has banes under his influence that dwell in the Underworld as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fomori are originally intended as cannon fodder for werewolves (one of the most powerful character types), and thus might be too strong for changelings (one of the weakest character types). However they do have ties to House Balor so there are perfectly good reasons to use them. </div> </div> </div> Fomori vary drastically in capabilities. Use one that would suit your chronicle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Demons are tricky. There isn't really a reason you couldn't...but it doesn't really jive with Demon. Fighting gross monsters just isn't what Demon is really about. </div> </div> </div> Have you read the Earthbound book its all about fighting gross monsters. Seriously Earthbound have rules for people with pus and wangs for bodies. But Fomori don't even have to be obscenely gross, they can be bestial, or just off. Demon already has infernal investments, but Book of the Wyrm has them as well. Earthbound investments often result in beings just like Fomori. And even normal demons can give thralls powers, and then mutate them with lore of Flesh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T01:10:07-07:00","id":104687,"title":"","content":"For me, they add nothing to the narrative of Vampire, and serve to detract from the most interesting antagonists of the setting, other Vampires.<br /> <br /> Spirits exist within the setting, but are hidden thngs that need to be sought out, encountering spirits in night clubs is simply too banal for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/919-harlokin","name":"harlokin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T01:16:30-07:00","id":104688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>harlokin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/104617-why-not-use-the-fomori-mockeries-in-all-the-gamelines?p=104687#post104687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, they add nothing to the narrative of Vampire, and serve to detract from the most interesting antagonists of the setting, other Vampires.<br /> <br /> Spirits exist within the setting, but are hidden thngs that need to be sought out, encountering spirits in night clubs is simply too banal for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then what about just restricting it to infernalists in your particular game? Tremere already bind demons into corpses, and make Homunculi to guard their Chantries. Sabbat have infernalists that make deals with demons for power.<br /> <br /> Like everything you find in the books you have to make it suit your specific games. Vozhd don't just trample Night Clubs willy nilly either.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T03:46:25-07:00","id":104744,"title":"","content":"I quite like the idea. I'd suggest that in the case of non-spiritual settings, Fomori are around - but not evidently so. They might be the morally flexible health executive making a deal with the Kindred to sell out their hospital's customers. The Kindred never needs to know that it's a Fomor, and the Fomor has no reason to show him that it is. Both just benefit from the deal.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm not sure how much they add to Masquerade or if they should ever come to the fore in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/836-obyrne","user":"Obyrne","date":". 04-03-2014, 06:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/836-obyrne","name":"Obyrne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T04:48:16-07:00","id":104756,"title":"","content":"Well it serves a good tool to make the sins of PCs come back to bite them in the Arse. A lot of time in vampire games the only negative consequence for doing really horrible things is your Humanity can be lowered, and sometimes not even that. But now say the business partner you Dominated into a broken half person gets possessed because they are little more then an empty shell and in getting possessed they go from tool you are used to abusing to an obstacle in your way.<br /> <br /> Or even victims of conventional malevolence, you get back at an enemy Kindred by shutting off the water in their apartment, a encouraging local criminals to target the area, maybe after a while all the suffering concentrated in the area draws spirits of violence to inhabit folks.<br /> <br /> Its something that isn't guaranteed to happen but they are events you can have happen to accentuate the repercussions of players actions. Simplest example is blood is addictive, and ghoul relationships are built on that simple fact. A good way to show the effects you have is to have them possessed literally by a spirit of addiction, perhaps even with powers to master the addiction of the PC who caused the whole mess.<br /> <br /> It would also serve a nice tool for indicating Sabbat Territory. Sabbat generally sow misery and chaos in the kine populace, and their foot print could be an upspike in random possessions. And like everything you can choose how often or rare you want these in your games.<br /> <br /> Another example of that is in Revised games in the antagonist section they often talk about revenants, ghosts inhabiting bodies that died of violence seeking revenge. They mention after the week of nightmares this has been happening more often. But its left open, you can run a whole game without bringing it up, but if you choose to use it in a game its no trouble, its just a sign of the times. Or really the same as ghost. Sometimes ghosts haunt places. Sometimes they don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T05:21:11-07:00","id":104770,"title":"","content":"I don't feel that human nature, and how it interacts with Vampirism in VtM, needs the addition of 'supernatural evil' possession to make it interesting or consequential.<br /> <br /> Thanks, but no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/919-harlokin","name":"harlokin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T06:35:20-07:00","id":104786,"title":"","content":"They don't do much to build on the narrative themes of Changeling, and can do a lot to detract from them. The big problem is that they're too self-evidently <i>real</i>. It becomes a lot harder to sell the idea that magic is fragile and precious as soon as you start crossing over with any entity that's not subject to Banality, or something similar. The <i>original</i> Fomori, and those Adhene, Thallain and Shadow Courtiers who may be affiliated with them, can serve similar purposes, while still being subject to the overall Changeling themes. Werewolf books may indicate a bigger link between their Bane-haunted monsters and the Elder Nightmares, but Changeling books seem to indicate that the Fianna just remembered the name of the latter and used it to describe the former, and that there's never been any deliberate collusion between them (although House Balor and some Thallain have made contacts on their own).<br /> <br /> Of all the other things in the WoD, Mages and Wraiths tend to be the easiest to cross into a Changeling game. Mages, because they're playing the <i>belief</i> and <i>imagination</i> angle from the other direction, and Wraiths because stories about being <i>forgotten </i>resonate strongly with both groups. Werewolves also have a lot of hooks to link up to Changelings, but that works a lot better from the Werewolf direction, sprinkling the dwindling fae in as another reminder of Gaia's decline and the Wyld's peril.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please add signature.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/615-the-hanged-man","name":"The Hanged Man","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T07:16:54-07:00","id":104799,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Depending on the game, I can see the appeal of using Fomori in a few games. <br /> <br /> Before I continue, I have given this zero thought \u2013 I\u2019m just throwing stuff out there\u2026<br /> <br /> Vampire: Again, depending on the game\u2026I could see these being thematically inappropriate to add. <br /> Or. <br /> Just awesome.<br /> I\u2019m thinking maybe a Level 4 -5 Koldunic Sorcery Ritual along the lines (mechanically) of that Goblin Spider web-formori-ritual from the Furry Super Sentai book. <br /> <br /> Mage: Meh. Why not.<br /> <br /> Changeling: Again, depending on the game. If you wanted to take that direction with House Balor, that might be an interesting way to go. That also might make an interesting \u201clesser of evils\u201d sort of game: a Motely of redcaps versus the monsters of House Balor.<br /> <br /> Wraith: Honestly, I\u2019m opposed to the idea of Fomori in Wraith. That\u2019s just me.<br /> <br /> Demon: As a Crossover (with a capitol C), I think Demon and Werewolf have some major cosmological differences that need counseling before they find a happy relationship together. Mechanically, it might take a little tweaking/meshing of enthrallment and fomori rules. Nothing too hefty. The mythos, on other hand, is where you might run into some wonkiness.<br /> <br /> Think I covered all the bases (and my opinions thereof). Off to get coffee\u2026</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T08:38:36-07:00","id":104849,"title":"","content":"Fomori as Fomori makes no sense at all in Changeling. Changelings have no dealings with the Umbra.<br /> <br /> Now, a mortal possessed by a particularly nasty nervosa works well. A jealous chimera childhood friend that doesn't want to let go when the child outgrows it fits perfectly. A scion of House Balor leading an army of corrupted mortals infected by the spores of a great fell beast, oh yes! Mortals having their minds dulled by some sort of banal chimera and commanded to lash out when they encounter anything of glamour also fits.<br /> <br /> So yeah, Werewolf: The Apocalypse Formori don't really have a place in Changeling, but possessed mortals with traits inspired by Fomori fit pretty perfectly as long as they're given that Changeling spin and not lifted straight from Werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T09:42:32-07:00","id":104888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/104617-why-not-use-the-fomori-mockeries-in-all-the-gamelines?p=104849#post104849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fomori as Fomori makes no sense at all in Changeling. Changelings have no dealings with the Umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aside from Nunnehi and Menehune, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T09:52:17-07:00","id":104898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/104617-why-not-use-the-fomori-mockeries-in-all-the-gamelines?p=104888#post104888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aside from Nunnehi and Menehune, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which was incredibly dumb and make no sense what so ever. Maybe the writers at the time forgot which gameline they were writing for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":